    ('45e14070-ea8b-576e-9c6c-76eef3fcee4e', '283807e9-7ebe-52cc-99ed-39e85856aaf9', $q$A program reads a config file that might be missing. If it is missing it should continue with defaults, and an opened file must always be closed. What is the best approach?$q$, 'CHOOSE_APPROACH', $o$["Catch Exception around all of main and ignore it", "Declare main throws Exception and let the program crash", "Check file.exists() once and never use try/catch", "try-with-resources, catching FileNotFoundException to fall back to defaults"]$o$, $a$try-with-resources, catching FileNotFoundException to fall back to defaults$a$, $e$try-with-resources closes the file automatically and a specific catch lets you recover only from the expected problem. Swallowing every Exception hides real bugs, and exists() alone can still race with the file disappearing.$e$, 15, 4, now(), now()),
