    ('3c0f1a79-a155-5791-a767-c7acf7193bac', '2b686611-27e8-527d-9b82-643df82d4514', $q$In a singly linked list where you already hold the head, how long does inserting a new node at the head take?$q$, 'MCQ', $o$["O(n), because elements must shift", "O(1)", "O(log n)", "O(n), because you walk to the end"]$o$, $a$O(1)$a$, $e$Create the node, point it at the old head and make it the new head: a constant number of steps. Shifting is an array cost and walking to the end is for tail insertion without a tail pointer.$e$, 10, 1, now(), now()),
