    ('c73d582f-e332-55fe-8278-b706ce300a18', '2b686611-27e8-527d-9b82-643df82d4514', $q$You must detect whether a linked list contains a cycle while using only O(1) extra memory. Which approach works?$q$, 'CHOOSE_APPROACH', $o$["Store every visited node in a HashSet", "Two pointers: slow moves 1 step, fast moves 2 steps", "Traverse until null and count the nodes", "Reverse the list and compare it to the original"]$o$, $a$Two pointers: slow moves 1 step, fast moves 2 steps$a$, $e$If a cycle exists the fast pointer eventually catches the slow one; if not, fast reaches null. The HashSet works but uses O(n) memory, and counting until null loops forever on a cycle.$e$, 15, 4, now(), now()),
