    ('c74b1d26-c24d-5bf5-99fa-c01faa90227e', '5391f6ce-444e-5a6f-a1de-ab72e5073d04', $q$What does it mean for a sorting algorithm to be stable?$q$, 'MCQ', $o$["It never throws an exception", "Elements that compare equal keep their original relative order", "It always runs in O(n) time", "It uses no extra memory"]$o$, $a$Elements that compare equal keep their original relative order$a$, $e$Stability matters when sorting records by one key after another, for example by name then by score. It says nothing about running time or memory.$e$, 10, 1, now(), now()),
