    ('c2b9ad4b-8103-5214-8a9a-11bd96e4f381', '5391f6ce-444e-5a6f-a1de-ab72e5073d04', $q$You must sort 5 million integers held in memory as fast as reliably possible. What do you use?$q$, 'CHOOSE_APPROACH', $o$["Bubble sort, because it is the simplest", "Insertion sort, because it is stable", "Selection sort, because it makes the fewest swaps", "A built-in O(n log n) sort such as Arrays.sort"]$o$, $a$A built-in O(n log n) sort such as Arrays.sort$a$, $e$O(n log n) sorts stay practical at millions of items, while bubble, insertion and selection sort are O(n^2) and would take far too long. Fewer swaps or stability do not rescue a quadratic algorithm.$e$, 15, 4, now(), now()),
