    ('a81cca19-10d4-5e88-95b3-e20f7e6bae92', 'a5bdc5a1-5107-58cb-89a7-f619fdbae310', $q$What does an inorder traversal of a binary search tree produce?$q$, 'MCQ', $o$["Values in ascending sorted order", "Values in descending sorted order", "Values level by level", "Values in the order they were inserted"]$o$, $a$Values in ascending sorted order$a$, $e$Inorder visits left subtree, node, then right subtree, and in a BST everything left is smaller and everything right is larger. Level order and insertion order are different things.$e$, 10, 1, now(), now()),
