    ('daf870da-feea-5c37-a686-4eff116b4544', '4e9d5695-d469-5b06-af81-a40b153f8697', $q$Which statement correctly describes a stack?$q$, 'MCQ', $o$["First in, first out: the oldest item is removed first", "Items are always removed in sorted order", "Last in, first out: the most recently pushed item is removed first", "Any item can be removed in constant time by its position"]$o$, $a$Last in, first out: the most recently pushed item is removed first$a$, $e$A stack only exposes its top, so push and pop work on the newest item. FIFO describes a queue, which is the tempting mix-up.$e$, 10, 1, now(), now()),
