    ('b992232a-63fd-538e-a3b7-06558953db6f', '0377fccd-d9d3-5370-8eb0-a8f1cc72b50f', $q$A queue is built on an ArrayList and dequeues with list.remove(0). What is the cost of one dequeue?$q$, 'MCQ', $o$["O(n), because every remaining element shifts one slot left", "O(1), because only the first element is touched", "O(log n), because the list is halved", "O(n^2), because each shift is itself a removal"]$o$, $a$O(n), because every remaining element shifts one slot left$a$, $e$Removing at index 0 of an array-backed list shifts all n-1 others. ArrayDeque or a circular buffer gives O(1) dequeue instead.$e$, 20, 5, now(), now()),
