    ('5c5fb61d-f52c-5297-ba33-29b439990e39', 'edc022a5-158a-5b8c-9186-f67fbb5d6db3', $q$Which pairing of traversal and helper structure is correct?$q$, 'MCQ', $o$["BFS uses a stack; DFS uses a queue", "BFS uses a queue; DFS uses a stack or recursion", "Both use a priority queue", "Both use a queue, but DFS marks nodes later"]$o$, $a$BFS uses a queue; DFS uses a stack or recursion$a$, $e$A queue processes nodes in discovery order, giving level-by-level BFS. A stack (or the call stack) dives deep first, which is DFS; swapping them turns one traversal into the other.$e$, 10, 1, now(), now()),
