    ('04c6643b-59aa-5ed9-95eb-ec7c9446512f', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001002', 'Payroll Polymorphism', $d$Read n employees, one per line. Kinds: FULL s (pay = s + s/10), PART h r (pay = h*r, plus ((h-40)*r)/2 extra if h > 40), CONTRACT d r (pay = d*r), INTERN (pay = 500). All divisions are integer divisions. Model them with an abstract class and subclasses, print each employee's pay on its own line, then a final line TOTAL followed by the sum.$d$, 'MEDIUM', 'JAVA', $i$Line 1: n. Next n lines: an employee record as described.$i$, $p$n lines with each pay, then one line 'TOTAL x'.$p$, $k$1 <= n <= 1000, all numbers are non-negative and at most 100000$k$,
